 {"version_id": "prompt-12", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Metamorphic and negative-case regression checks", "target_failure_mode": "Edge-case and regression handling", "expected_dimension": "reasoning_soundness", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, first perform repository reconnaissance: locate the primary implementation, all callers, related subclasses or alternate backends, existing regression tests, and analogous behavior elsewhere in the repository.", "replace": "Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, identify the behavior-preserving relations that should remain true, such as equivalent representations producing equivalent results, repeated operations remaining stable, and unrelated parameters not changing the result. Test the requested case plus negative cases, boundary transitions, invalid inputs, and nearby legacy cases. Pay special at"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.86, "reasoning_soundness": 0.83, "execution_accuracy": 0.82, "output_integrity": 0.88}, "aggregate": 0.8475, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.32}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.31}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "proposed_not_applied", "apply_note": "find-block matched 0x (need exactly 1)", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0125, "why": "Metamorphic and negative checks help expose regressions that ordinary examples miss, particularly around repeated operations and unrelated parameters. The approach is less directly actionable than a focused reproduction or layered triage and risks assuming invalid behavior-preserving relations, keeping gains modest."}
 {"version_id": "prompt-13", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Evidence-chain localization with explicit hypothesis testing", "target_failure_mode": "Complex repository-specific diagnosis and implementation", "expected_dimension": "reasoning_soundness", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, perform evidence-gated repository localization.", "replace": "Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, perform evidence-gated repository localization: first write a short hypothesis about the failure, then verify it by tracing the reported input through the concrete call chain to the failing output. Record the exact files, symbols, and conditions that confirm or falsify the hypothesis; do not commit to a fix based only on similarly named code"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.89, "reasoning_soundness": 0.87, "execution_accuracy": 0.82, "output_integrity": 0.88}, "aggregate": 0.865, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.29}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.27}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.03, "why": "Evidence-gated localization and explicit hypothesis testing directly address repository-specific diagnosis, improving reasoning and execution on the difficult Django and Astropy cases. The method is disciplined but does not by itself add substantial regression validation, so gains over baseline are moderate."}
 {"version_id": "prompt-14", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Change-surface and compatibility mapping", "target_failure_mode": "Complex repository-specific diagnosis and implementation", "expected_dimension": "target_alignment", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "Identify the primary implementation, every relevant caller, subclasses, alternate backends, serializers/parsers, configuration defaults, and existing regression tests.", "replace": "Identify the primary implementation and construct a change-surface map covering every relevant caller, subclass or override, alternate backend, serializer/parser, configuration default, public API boundary, and existing regression test. For each item, state whether the proposed behavior must change, must remain unchanged, or needs a compatibility test; use repository search to verify the map befor"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.88, "reasoning_soundness": 0.86, "execution_accuracy": 0.78, "output_integrity": 0.88}, "aggregate": 0.85, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.94}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.94}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.24}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.22}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.015, "why": "Compatibility mapping is relevant to complex framework changes and improves awareness of callers and public boundaries. However, the exhaustive change-surface inventory can encourage speculative edits and diffuse execution, producing a small regression below baseline on simpler probes and only limited improvement on the hardest cases."}
